# SHAPE3 - CHUTE3.md's scratch course (docs/plans/bonanza-courses/CHUTE3.md): the PROTOTYPE `chute 3` on a plate,
# the way shapes.bbc lays the 1- and 2-wide ones.  NOT a shipped course and in no build: compile it by hand,
#   python3 tools/bbcourse.py docs/plans/bonanza-courses/chute3/shape3.bbc -o <dir> --png <dir>
# Back to front:
#  - a 3-WIDE `round` chute 10 px deep, up, right and down: two radial corners turning the same way;
#  - a 3-WIDE `bank` chute 8 px deep, the same shape, its second leg CLIMBING 1.5 units to a raised corner
#    and its third FALLING back to the plate;
#  - in front, a 3-WIDE `round` chute 10 px deep, an S: corners turning BOTH ways (it adds no table).
course SHP3 "Shape Test 3"
music fairway
width  128
origin 480
ball   rubber

floor rect   4  3 31 25  flat 2
chute 3 round depth 10 way  9 10 2 way  9 5 way 16 5 way 16 10
chute 3 bank  depth 8  way 22 10 2 way 22 5 way 28 5 3.5 way 28 10 2
chute 3 round depth 10 way  6 16 2 way 14 16 way 14 21 way 22 21

start 5 4
goal  tile 30 24  flat 2
clock 28 24
target 60
way 5 4
way 9 11
way 9 10
way 9 6
